      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My personal take on this:\n\n> It would be better off if we were to receive a warning of what TOS we are breaking before getting banned\n\nThe bans are not permanent on first offense (for most cases I've seen). VRChat is important for a lot of people, and to me personally it seems like the Trust and Safety team understands this. Proportional, transparent, and consistent short 1-7 day suspensions serve as an effective warning on its own, while leaving the door open for return. It signals seriousness on the matter.\n\nA warning could signal indifference or lack of seriousness, a lack of repercussions for violating ToS, which to me sounds like to be something OP perceives to be an issue to be dealt with: an oxymoron.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "697c1408ed63ba9b2f99f1c8",
      "aiGenerated": false,
