      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Less important rambling:\n\n> there are some TOS that can be accidentally broken.\n\nHuh? Users need to explicitly click to agree to the up-to-date Terms of Service before being let in to VRChat.\n\nIf I recall correctly, there's also a random loading screen tip for [Community Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/community-guidelines).\n\nThere's also the [Developer Update - December 18 2025](https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-december-18-2025/47354) which clarifies how to not get bopped (probably).\n\nThere's also a reason in the ban message, referring to the community guideline which got the user bopped, so that the user can read and/or take corrective steps to avoid getting bopped again.\n\n> People who try their best to abide by the TOS are getting punished while the ones who break it the most face no repercussions.\n\nI'm no Strasz, but this seems to be simply untrue. The moderation system relies on user reports. If an user got bopped, it's most likely because some other VRChat user reported the action or didn't consent to it - or vice versa, nothing may happen without a report.\n\nThe feature request in OP also seems to advocate for having no initial seriousness or repercussions for an offense for breaking the ToS, so this seems like an oxymoron.\n\n> Accidentally pressing the \"Public\" button thinking it's making it private. \n\nIs this about instances or the worlds/avatars SDK? In the SDK, \"Private\" is the default option in dropdown menu; for instances, \"Join\" defaults to Public. Due to the height of Public/Friends+/Friends/Invite+/Invite/Group buttons, it is hard to misclick \"Public\" for new instances imo.\n\n> Forgetting to add proper tags to avatars. \n\nFair; also SDK overwriting tags sometimes (due to bugs or old cached information).\n\nMy workflow makes it necessary to visit VRChat Home website to generate impostors, set gallery images and acknowledgements on new avatars anyway, so it's part of important due diligence to set tags (a second chance if initially missed in the SDK).\n\nWhat would you suggest to improve this issue?\n\n> Unsure what exactly is \"Sexual Content\" in VRChat's eyes\n\nThis is mostly outlined in the [Creator Guidelines](https://hello.vrchat.com/creator-guidelines) and Developer Update - December 18 2025.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
