      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> You could make a documentation system where you file down who got warnings and who got banned and for what reasons. \n\nI'm guessing detailed information about individual users cannot be shared for privacy reasons, most likely. I'm sure the transparency on what's allowed or not allowed by example could be expanded or improved, but right now the Developer Update - December 18 2025 and Community/Creator Guidelines are the best we can have to explain how the Terms of Service are enforced.\n\nIf you legitimately report content/behavior on VRChat, when done right you may also learn quickly what may be allowable or prohibited (an attacker-defender scenario), how the guidelines are enforced at VRChat.\n\n> Getting banned and no way of appealing cause technically it was breaking TOS\n\nAppealing is still plausible at https://vrch.at/moderation.\n\n> People who follow TOS the best they can get banned while the ones who go out of their way to break them stay without punishment\n\nAgain I'm no Stratz on reddit, but this seems to be simply untrue; the moderation relies on user reports and human review.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
