  "details": "It would be better off if we were to receive a warning of what TOS we are breaking before getting banned as there are some TOS that can be accidentally broken. Making a way to get warned on the actual application will give those who are accidentally breaking TOS and those who didn't care in the first place wouldn't change the problem and would get banned as they should.\n\nPeople who try their best to abide by the TOS are getting punished while the ones who break it the most face no repercussions. You could make a documentation system where you file down who got warnings and who got banned and for what reasons. \n\nWays you can accidentally break TOS:\n\nAccidentally pressing the \"Public\" button thinking it's making it private. \n\nForgetting to add proper tags to avatars. \n\nUnsure what exactly is \"Sexual Content\" in VRChat's eyes\n\n(I myself had issues like these as I am autistic and take things literal and to the point. What VRChat considered Sexual isn't what I did; so I had no clue until it was too late and the same has happened to some of my friends as well. )\n\nGetting banned and no way of appealing cause technically it was breaking TOS makes things harder on those who try to follow the TOS and discourage the one following the rules. People who follow TOS the best they can get banned while the ones who go out of their way to break them stay without punishment, please do something about this.",
